WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.840
some of the coolest examples&nbsp;
of the use of crowdsourcing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:10.320
in places you would not expect come from&nbsp;
nasa the space agency in the u.s has used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:15.360
open innovation and crowdsourcing systematically&nbsp;
for the past decade they have learned to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.760
open innovation to solve problems in the&nbsp;
space station to help think about how to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:26.400
keep astronauts safe and healthy while they're&nbsp;
in space and even how to deal with space poo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:32.000
so nasa has thought a lot about how to&nbsp;
incorporate open innovation into their processes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:39.120
another cool example comes from the defense&nbsp;
department in the u.s where they actually started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:46.080
challenges to help create the autonomous driving&nbsp;
revolution that all of us will be seeing over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:54.480
next few decades they started challenges and and&nbsp;
and contests to enable anybody from around the us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.480 --> 00:01:00.640
to participate and create solutions to creating&nbsp;
software and robots that could allow cars to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:07.920
travel on their own so in key key areas space&nbsp;
exploration for humanity autonomous driving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:22.320
open innovation has played an important role&nbsp;
in unlocking innovation from around the world

